{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================================
  GOD SQUAD — brand-values.liquid

  The brand values strip: a row of glyph / title / subtitle tiles, sitting
  directly above the footer on every page.

  WHY THIS IS A SECTION AND NOT A BLOCK ON footer.liquid. Every block that
  section emits lands inside `.footer__blocks`, which is a grid of COLUMNS
  (section-footer.css:62-65). A value arm would render as one more column beside
  the menus, never as a full-width strip above them, and forcing it out would
  mean two filtered passes over section.blocks — which decouples the Theme
  Editor's drag order from the DOM while block.shopify_attributes still claims to
  bind it. footer.liquid's block budget is also already spent: link_list 4 plus
  text 2 is exactly the six PHASE-2:2526 permits per section.

  It lives in sections/footer-group.json rather than templates/index.json so it
  reaches every page, which is what the approved design shows. PHASE-2 §29.1
  named this section `brand-values` before it was built; §29.5 specifies its
  settings, its blocks and its spacing, and this follows that specification
  rather than inventing one.

  THE DARK-ON-DARK JOIN IS THE ONE THE SYSTEM ALLOWS. PHASE-2 §26.4 rule 5:
  "Values sits directly under Our Story, both dark. This is the only permitted
  dark-on-dark join, and it is marked by border-top and border-bottom." The same
  applies here, where it sits above a dark footer — hence both edges, at
  --color-border, and the `show_dividers` switch that owns all three hairlines.
  ============================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign heading = section.settings.heading | strip

  assign surface_class = 'surface-dark'
  if section.settings.surface == 'light'
    assign surface_class = 'surface-light'
  endif

  comment
    A tile with no title and no glyph is not a tile. On the live storefront it is
    skipped; in the Theme Editor every block renders, because a block that emits
    nothing emits no shopify_attributes either, and the editor then has no
    element to outline or scroll to when the merchant clicks Add value.
  endcomment

  comment
    columns_desktop is a CEILING, not a promise -- PHASE-2 29.5 states it that
    way and the setting's own info repeats it. Three values in a four-column
    grid leaves an empty fourth column and shoves the row off-centre, which is
    what the first render of this strip did. Take the smaller of the two.
  endcomment
  assign cols = section.settings.columns_desktop
  if section.blocks.size > 0 and section.blocks.size < cols
    assign cols = section.blocks.size
  endif

  assign classes = 'brand-values '
  assign classes = classes | append: surface_class
  assign classes = classes | append: ' brand-values--cols-' | append: cols
  if section.settings.show_dividers
    assign classes = classes | append: ' brand-values--dividers'
  endif
-%}

{%- if section.blocks.size == 0 and request.design_mode == false -%}
  {%- comment -%} Not configured yet: render nothing, and request nothing. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- else -%}

{{ 'section-brand-values.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<div class="{{ classes }}">
  <div class="brand-values__inner container">
    {%- if heading != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Left-aligned, because PHASE-2 §26.3 rule 1 makes every editorial band
        left-aligned and permits centring in exactly two places: inside a product
        card and inside a value TILE. The tiles below are centred; this heading
        is not.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <h2 class="brand-values__heading">{{ heading | escape }}</h2>
    {%- endif -%}

    <ul class="brand-values__list" role="list">
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign title = block.settings.title | strip
          assign sub = block.settings.sub | strip
          assign icon = block.settings.icon
          assign url = block.settings.link

          assign is_empty = false
          if title == blank and sub == blank
            assign is_empty = true
          endif
        -%}
        {%- if is_empty and request.design_mode == false -%}
          {%- continue -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          A case, not `{% render 'icon-' | append: icon %}`. The render tag takes
          a STRING LITERAL for the snippet name — a variable will not resolve and
          a filter cannot be applied to a render argument at all. Captured once
          so the linked and unlinked tiles below share it rather than repeating
          the whole dispatch twice.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- capture icon_html -%}
          {%- case icon -%}
            {%- when 'crown' -%}{% render 'icon-crown', class: 'brand-values__icon' %}
            {%- when 'community' -%}{% render 'icon-community', class: 'brand-values__icon' %}
            {%- when 'globe' -%}{% render 'icon-globe', class: 'brand-values__icon' %}
            {%- when 'diamond' -%}{% render 'icon-diamond', class: 'brand-values__icon' %}
          {%- endcase -%}
        {%- endcapture -%}

        <li
          class="brand-values__item{% if is_empty %} brand-values__item--empty{% endif %}"
          {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
        >
          {%- comment -%}
            The whole tile is the target when a link is set, so the anchor is the
            tile's padded box rather than a word inside it — the padding lives on
            the anchor for that reason, not on the <li>.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if url != blank -%}
            <a class="brand-values__body" href="{{ url }}">
              {{ icon_html }}
              {%- if title != blank -%}
                <span class="brand-values__title">{{ title | escape }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if sub != blank -%}
                <span class="brand-values__sub">{{ sub | escape }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </a>
          {%- else -%}
            <div class="brand-values__body">
              {{ icon_html }}
              {%- if title != blank -%}
                <span class="brand-values__title">{{ title | escape }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if sub != blank -%}
                <span class="brand-values__sub">{{ sub | escape }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>

    {%- if request.design_mode -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign notices = ''
        if section.blocks.size == 0
          assign notices = notices | append: 'no_blocks|'
        endif
        assign no_icon = 0
        for block in section.blocks
          if block.settings.icon == blank or block.settings.icon == 'none'
            assign no_icon = no_icon | plus: 1
          endif
        endfor
        if no_icon > 0
          assign notices = notices | append: 'no_icon|'
        endif
      -%}
      {%- if notices != blank -%}
        <div class="brand-values__notice">
          {%- if notices contains 'no_blocks' -%}
            <p>{{ 'sections.brand_values.no_blocks' | t }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if notices contains 'no_icon' -%}
            <p>{{ 'sections.brand_values.no_icon' | t }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Brand values",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "brand-values-section",
  "max_blocks": 6,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "info": "Optional. The strip reads as chrome without one."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "columns_desktop",
      "label": "Columns on desktop",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 4,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 4,
      "info": "A ceiling, not a promise: fewer values than this show fewer columns."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_dividers",
      "label": "Show hairline dividers",
      "info": "The rules above, below and between the tiles.",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "surface",
      "label": "Surface",
      "options": [
        { "value": "dark", "label": "Ink" },
        { "value": "light", "label": "Cream" }
      ],
      "default": "dark"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "value",
      "name": "Value",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "icon",
          "label": "Glyph",
          "options": [
            { "value": "none", "label": "None" },
            { "value": "crown", "label": "Crown" },
            { "value": "community", "label": "Community" },
            { "value": "globe", "label": "Globe" },
            { "value": "diamond", "label": "Diamond" }
          ],
          "default": "crown"
        },
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "sub", "label": "Subtitle" },
        {
          "type": "url",
          "id": "link",
          "label": "Link",
          "info": "Optional. With a link the whole tile becomes one target."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Brand values",
      "settings": {
        "columns_desktop": 4,
        "show_dividers": true,
        "surface": "dark"
      },
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "value", "settings": { "icon": "crown", "title": "Faith Driven", "sub": "More Than Clothing" } },
        { "type": "value", "settings": { "icon": "community", "title": "Community", "sub": "People With Purpose" } },
        { "type": "value", "settings": { "icon": "diamond", "title": "Premium Quality", "sub": "Crafted To Inspire" } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
